Make-Blog "tax-consultant-doctors-pakistan" "Tax Consultant for Doctors in Pakistan 2026" "Expert tax consultant for doctors and medical professionals in Pakistan. NTN registration, income tax return filing, clinic income tax, FBR compliance for MBBS, specialist and hospital owners." "2027-03-28" "Tax Guides" "Medical Professionals Tax" '<p class="article-lead">Kamboh Associates provides dedicated tax and FBR compliance services for doctors, consultants, and medical professionals across Pakistan. Whether you run a private clinic, work in a hospital, or practice as a specialist, your income tax obligations are specific and different from a salaried employee. Our team handles everything from NTN registration to annual returns and wealth statements.</p><h2 id="overview">Tax Obligations for Doctors in Pakistan</h2><p>Doctors in Pakistan fall under the self-employed or professional income category. If you receive fee income from a private clinic, patients, or hospital consultancy, this is professional income taxable under the Income Tax Ordinance 2001. Hospital employers often deduct withholding tax at source, but you are still required to file an annual income tax return and declare all income and assets in your wealth statement.</p><div class="info-box"><i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i><p><strong>Key Point:</strong> Doctors who have been deducted withholding tax by hospitals may still owe additional tax if their total income from all sources exceeds the basic exemption threshold. Filing ensures you avoid FBR notices and maintain active filer status.</p></div><h2 id="obligations">What Taxes Apply to Doctors</h2><ul><li><strong>Income Tax on Professional Fee</strong> - Clinic consultation fees, procedure charges, and private practice income are all taxable</li><li><strong>Withholding Tax by Hospitals</strong> - Hospitals deduct tax at source on payments to visiting consultants; this must be reconciled in your annual return</li><li><strong>Wealth Statement</strong> - All assets including property, vehicles, savings, and investments must be declared annually</li><li><strong>Sales Tax (if applicable)</strong> - If annual clinic turnover exceeds Rs 10 million, sales tax registration may be required</li><li><strong>Advance Tax</strong> - Doctors whose tax liability exceeds a threshold must pay advance tax in quarterly installments</li></ul><div class="info-grid"><div class="info-card"><div class="label">NTN Registration</div><div class="value">Rs 1,500</div><div class="sub">24-48 hours</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Tax Return Filing</div><div class="value">From Rs 5,000</div><div class="sub">Professional income</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Wealth Statement</div><div class="value">From Rs 5,000</div><div class="sub">2-3 days</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Filing Deadline</div><div class="value">30 September</div><div class="sub">Each tax year</div></div></div><h2 id="services">Our Services for Doctors</h2><ul><li><strong>NTN Registration</strong> - Get your tax number in 24-48 hours</li><li><strong>Annual Income Tax Return</strong> - Correct treatment of clinic income, hospital WHT, and other income</li><li><strong>Wealth Statement Preparation</strong> - Accurate declaration of property, savings, vehicles, and investments</li><li><strong>FBR Notice Response</strong> - Professional handling of any tax demand or audit notice</li><li><strong>Advance Tax Planning</strong> - Calculate and pay advance tax correctly to avoid penalties</li><li><strong>Sales Tax Registration</strong> - If your clinic turnover requires it</li></ul><h2 id="pricing">Pricing</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Price</th><th>Timeline</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>NTN Registration</td><td>From Rs 1,500</td><td>24-48 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Professional Income Tax Return</td><td>From Rs 5,000</td><td>1-2 days</td></tr><tr><td>Wealth Statement</td><td>From Rs 5,000</td><td>2-3 days</td></tr><tr><td>FBR Notice Response</td><td>From Rs 5,000</td><td>24-48 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Sales Tax Registration</td><td>From Rs 5,000</td><td>7-14 days</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="article-cta"><h3>Tax Help for Doctors - Get Started Today</h3><p>WhatsApp your details to 0328-4675162 and our tax consultants handle your FBR compliance professionally. Free first consultation.</p><div class="cta-btns"><a href="https://wa.me/923284675162?text=Hi%2C+I+am+a+doctor+and+need+tax+help." class="cta-btn-white" target="_blank"><i class="fab fa-whatsapp"></i> Free Consultation</a><a href="tel:03284675162" class="cta-btn-ghost"><i class="fas fa-phone"></i> 0328-4675162</a></div></div><h2 id="faqs">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">Do doctors need to file an income tax return in Pakistan? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Yes. All doctors with NTN or income above the basic exemption threshold must file an annual income tax return by 30 September. Even if WHT was deducted by a hospital, a return is required to declare all income sources and maintain active filer status.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">What income do I need to declare as a doctor? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">All income must be declared: clinic consultation fees, hospital salary or consultancy payments, procedure income, rent from property, bank profit, dividends, and any other source. Under-declaration is a risk FBR actively pursues through data matching.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">How much income tax does a doctor pay in Pakistan? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Doctors pay progressive income tax rates based on total annual income. The slab ranges from 0% (below Rs 600,000) to 35% (above Rs 6 million) for individuals. A qualified consultant ensures all deductions are maximized to reduce the tax liability legally.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">Can Kamboh Associates handle my tax return remotely? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Yes. Simply WhatsApp your CNIC and income details to 0328-4675162. We prepare and file your return entirely online without requiring an office visit.</div></div></div>'

Make-Blog "tax-consultant-lawyers-pakistan" "Tax Consultant for Lawyers in Pakistan 2026" "Expert tax consultant for lawyers and advocates in Pakistan. Income tax return filing on legal fee income, NTN registration, FBR compliance for barristers, advocates and law firms." "2027-03-29" "Tax Guides" "Legal Professionals Tax" '<p class="article-lead">Kamboh Associates provides specialist tax and FBR compliance services for lawyers, advocates, barristers, and law firms across Pakistan. Legal professionals earn professional income that carries specific tax treatment under the Income Tax Ordinance 2001. We handle your NTN registration, annual returns, and wealth statements with full accuracy.</p><h2 id="overview">Tax Obligations for Lawyers in Pakistan</h2><p>Lawyers and advocates practicing in Pakistan are classified as self-employed professionals. All fee income, retainer income, consultancy charges, and court appearance fees are taxable as professional income. Additionally, lawyers who engage articled clerks or employ staff may have employer withholding tax obligations.</p><div class="info-box"><i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i><p><strong>Key Point:</strong> Many lawyers believe that filing is optional if they receive cash fees with no WHT deducted. This is incorrect. Any lawyer with income exceeding the basic exemption or owning property, vehicles, or a bank account is required to file annually and maintain filer status.</p></div><h2 id="obligations">Tax Obligations for Legal Professionals</h2><ul><li><strong>Professional Fee Income Tax</strong> - All court fees, retainers, and legal consultancy payments are taxable</li><li><strong>Withholding Tax on Law Firm Payments</strong> - Payments made by corporate clients carry WHT obligations; these must be reconciled</li><li><strong>Wealth Statement</strong> - Chamber equipment, vehicles, property, and savings must all be declared</li><li><strong>Partners in Law Firms</strong> - AOP (Association of Persons) tax rules apply to partnerships</li><li><strong>Employer WHT if applicable</strong> - Deduct and deposit WHT on salaries paid to staff</li></ul><div class="info-grid"><div class="info-card"><div class="label">NTN Registration</div><div class="value">Rs 1,500</div><div class="sub">24-48 hours</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Tax Return</div><div class="value">From Rs 5,000</div><div class="sub">Professional income</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">AOP Return</div><div class="value">From Rs 8,000</div><div class="sub">Partnership firms</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Deadline</div><div class="value">30 September</div><div class="sub">Each tax year</div></div></div><h2 id="services">Our Services for Lawyers</h2><ul><li><strong>NTN Registration</strong> - For individual advocates and law firms</li><li><strong>Individual and AOP Tax Returns</strong> - Sole practitioners and partnerships</li><li><strong>Wealth Statement</strong> - Accurate annual declaration</li><li><strong>FBR Notice Response</strong> - Professional representation</li><li><strong>Employer WHT Compliance</strong> - Monthly filing if you have staff</li></ul><h2 id="pricing">Pricing</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Price</th><th>Timeline</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>NTN Registration</td><td>From Rs 1,500</td><td>24-48 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Professional Income Tax Return</td><td>From Rs 5,000</td><td>1-2 days</td></tr><tr><td>AOP / Law Firm Return</td><td>From Rs 8,000</td><td>2-3 days</td></tr><tr><td>Wealth Statement</td><td>From Rs 5,000</td><td>2-3 days</td></tr><tr><td>FBR Notice Response</td><td>From Rs 5,000</td><td>24-48 hours</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="article-cta"><h3>Tax Help for Lawyers - Free Consultation</h3><p>WhatsApp your CNIC to 0328-4675162. Our consultants handle your FBR filing professionally and on time.</p><div class="cta-btns"><a href="https://wa.me/923284675162?text=Hi%2C+I+am+a+lawyer+and+need+tax+help." class="cta-btn-white" target="_blank"><i class="fab fa-whatsapp"></i> Free Consultation</a><a href="tel:03284675162" class="cta-btn-ghost"><i class="fas fa-phone"></i> 0328-4675162</a></div></div><h2 id="faqs">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">Are lawyers required to file income tax in Pakistan? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Yes. Lawyers with income above the exemption threshold, or those who own property, vehicles, or bank accounts, must file annually by 30 September. FBR cross-references Bar Council records to identify non-filing advocates.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">How is a law partnership taxed in Pakistan? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">A law firm partnership is taxed as an AOP (Association of Persons). The firm files a separate return at AOP rates and each partner also files individually, declaring their share of profit.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">What is the income tax rate for lawyers in Pakistan 2026? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Individual lawyers pay progressive rates from 0% to 35% depending on total annual income. AOPs pay a flat rate. A qualified consultant ensures deductions are maximized to minimize tax legally.</div></div></div>'

Make-Blog "tax-consultant-engineers-pakistan" "Tax Consultant for Engineers in Pakistan 2026" "Expert tax consultant for engineers in Pakistan. Income tax on engineering consultancy, project fees, salaried engineers, NTN registration, FBR return filing for civil, mechanical and IT engineers." "2027-03-30" "Tax Guides" "Engineering Professionals Tax" '<p class="article-lead">Kamboh Associates provides professional tax and FBR compliance services for engineers across Pakistan, including civil, mechanical, electrical, structural, and IT engineers. Whether you are salaried, self-employed, or running a consultancy firm, your tax obligations require expert handling to remain compliant and avoid penalties.</p><h2 id="overview">Tax Obligations for Engineers in Pakistan</h2><p>Engineers in Pakistan fall into two main categories for tax purposes: salaried employees and self-employed consultants. Salaried engineers in companies have WHT deducted by their employer, but must still file an annual return declaring all income. Self-employed engineers and consultancy firm owners must also register for NTN, file returns on their professional income, and submit a wealth statement.</p><div class="info-box"><i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i><p><strong>Important for Project-Based Engineers:</strong> Engineers who work on multiple projects across different companies often have WHT deducted by each client. All of these must be reconciled in your annual return. Any excess WHT deducted is refundable through FBR IRIS.</p></div><h2 id="obligations">Tax Categories for Engineers</h2><ul><li><strong>Salaried Engineers</strong> - WHT deducted by employer; must file return to declare total income and claim refund if applicable</li><li><strong>Consultancy Fee Income</strong> - Professional fees from projects are taxable at progressive slab rates</li><li><strong>Engineering Firm Partners</strong> - AOP tax rules apply to engineering partnerships</li><li><strong>Construction Contractors</strong> - Special withholding tax rules apply to contract payments</li><li><strong>IT Engineers / Software</strong> - May qualify for IT export income tax exemption under FBR rules</li></ul><div class="info-grid"><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Salaried Return</div><div class="value">Rs 3,500</div><div class="sub">Same day filing</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Consultancy Return</div><div class="value">From Rs 5,000</div><div class="sub">1-2 days</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Firm Return (AOP)</div><div class="value">From Rs 8,000</div><div class="sub">2-3 days</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Deadline</div><div class="value">30 September</div><div class="sub">Each tax year</div></div></div><h2 id="services">Our Services for Engineers</h2><ul><li><strong>NTN Registration</strong> - For individuals and engineering firms</li><li><strong>Salaried and Consultancy Tax Returns</strong> - Correct treatment of all income types</li><li><strong>Wealth Statement Preparation</strong> - Annual asset declaration</li><li><strong>WHT Reconciliation</strong> - Match all project WHT deductions to your IRIS records</li><li><strong>FBR Notice Response</strong> - Fast professional handling</li></ul><h2 id="pricing">Pricing</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Price</th><th>Timeline</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>NTN Registration</td><td>From Rs 1,500</td><td>24-48 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Salaried Return</td><td>From Rs 3,500</td><td>Same day</td></tr><tr><td>Consultancy Return</td><td>From Rs 5,000</td><td>1-2 days</td></tr><tr><td>AOP / Firm Return</td><td>From Rs 8,000</td><td>2-3 days</td></tr><tr><td>Wealth Statement</td><td>From Rs 5,000</td><td>2-3 days</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="article-cta"><h3>Tax Help for Engineers - Get Started</h3><p>WhatsApp 0328-4675162 with your CNIC and income details. We file your return quickly and accurately.</p><div class="cta-btns"><a href="https://wa.me/923284675162?text=Hi%2C+I+am+an+engineer+and+need+tax+help." class="cta-btn-white" target="_blank"><i class="fab fa-whatsapp"></i> Free Consultation</a><a href="tel:03284675162" class="cta-btn-ghost"><i class="fas fa-phone"></i> 0328-4675162</a></div></div><h2 id="faqs">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">Does a salaried engineer need to file a tax return in Pakistan? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Yes. Even if your employer deducts WHT, you must file an annual return by 30 September to declare total income, submit a wealth statement, and maintain active ATL filer status.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">Can engineers claim WHT refunds from multiple projects? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Yes. All WHT deducted by project clients appears in your FBR IRIS account. If excess tax was withheld beyond your actual liability, you can claim a refund through your annual return.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">Do IT engineers qualify for income tax exemption? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">IT software and services exported by registered freelancers and IT companies may qualify for income tax exemption or reduced rates under FBR IT export policy. Contact us to assess your eligibility.</div></div></div>'

Make-Blog "tax-consultant-government-employees-pakistan" "Tax Consultant for Government Employees Pakistan 2026" "Tax filing guide for government employees in Pakistan 2026. Income tax return for federal and provincial government servants, pension income, gratuity tax, NTN registration." "2027-03-31" "Tax Guides" "Government Employee Tax" '<p class="article-lead">Kamboh Associates provides expert income tax filing services for government employees across Pakistan, including federal, provincial, and semi-government servants. Government salaries have WHT deducted by the accounts department, but filing an annual return is still mandatory for all employees earning above the basic exemption. We handle your NTN registration, return filing, and wealth statements efficiently.</p><h2 id="overview">Do Government Employees Need to File Tax Returns?</h2><p>Yes. The Income Tax Ordinance 2001 requires all individuals with taxable income to file an annual tax return, regardless of whether their employer has already deducted WHT. Government employees who own property, vehicles, or have bank accounts above certain thresholds are specifically required to be on the ATL. Failure to file results in non-filer status, which increases withholding tax on all financial transactions.</p><div class="info-box"><i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i><p><strong>Good News for Government Employees:</strong> Filing is straightforward for salaried individuals with a single income source. The entire process takes less than 24 hours when you WhatsApp your salary certificate, CNIC, and asset details to 0328-4675162. Filing fee starts at just Rs 3,500.</p></div><h2 id="obligations">Tax Obligations for Government Servants</h2><ul><li><strong>Annual Income Tax Return</strong> - Due 30 September every year; declare salary, pension, rental, and other income</li><li><strong>Wealth Statement</strong> - Mandatory if you own property, vehicles, savings, or investments</li><li><strong>Pension Income</strong> - Monthly pension is taxable above the exemption limit; full pension up to Rs 1.5 million per year is exempt</li><li><strong>Gratuity and Commutation</strong> - Special tax rules apply; government commutation is generally exempt</li><li><strong>Rental Income</strong> - If you earn rent from property, it must be declared separately</li></ul><div class="info-grid"><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Salaried Return</div><div class="value">Rs 3,500</div><div class="sub">Same day filing</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">With Rental Income</div><div class="value">From Rs 5,000</div><div class="sub">1-2 days</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Wealth Statement</div><div class="value">From Rs 5,000</div><div class="sub">2-3 days</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Deadline</div><div class="value">30 September</div><div class="sub">Each tax year</div></div></div><h2 id="services">Our Services for Government Employees</h2><ul><li><strong>NTN Registration</strong> - Get your tax number in 24-48 hours</li><li><strong>Annual Salaried Tax Return</strong> - Quick and accurate filing</li><li><strong>Pension Income Tax Filing</strong> - Correct exemption application</li><li><strong>Wealth Statement</strong> - Full asset declaration</li><li><strong>Rental Income Declaration</strong> - Correct tax treatment</li></ul><h2 id="pricing">Pricing</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Price</th><th>Timeline</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>NTN Registration</td><td>From Rs 1,500</td><td>24-48 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Salaried Return (basic)</td><td>From Rs 3,500</td><td>Same day</td></tr><tr><td>Salary + Rental Income</td><td>From Rs 5,000</td><td>1-2 days</td></tr><tr><td>Wealth Statement</td><td>From Rs 5,000</td><td>2-3 days</td></tr><tr><td>Pension Return</td><td>From Rs 3,500</td><td>Same day</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="article-cta"><h3>Government Employee Tax Filing - Simple and Fast</h3><p>WhatsApp your salary certificate and CNIC to 0328-4675162. We file your return same day. Starts at Rs 3,500.</p><div class="cta-btns"><a href="https://wa.me/923284675162?text=Hi%2C+I+am+a+government+employee+and+need+tax+help." class="cta-btn-white" target="_blank"><i class="fab fa-whatsapp"></i> Free Consultation</a><a href="tel:03284675162" class="cta-btn-ghost"><i class="fas fa-phone"></i> 0328-4675162</a></div></div><h2 id="faqs">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">Is it compulsory for government employees to file income tax? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Yes. FBR requires all individuals with taxable income or assets to file annually. Government employees whose departments deduct WHT must still file to maintain filer status and avoid non-filer penalties on property, banking, and vehicle transactions.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">Is government pension taxable in Pakistan? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Government pension is exempt from income tax up to Rs 1.5 million per year under the Income Tax Ordinance. Above this threshold, the excess is taxable. Commutation of pension received as a lump sum is generally fully exempt for government servants.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">What documents do I need to file my tax return as a government employee? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">You need your CNIC copy, salary certificate or last pay slip (showing WHT deducted), details of any other income (rent, bank profit), and a list of assets. WhatsApp these to 0328-4675162 and we complete the filing for you.</div></div></div>'

Make-Blog "tax-filing-pensioners-pakistan" "Income Tax Return for Pensioners in Pakistan 2026" "Complete guide to income tax filing for pensioners and retired persons in Pakistan 2026. Is pension taxable? Exemption limits, FBR return process, NTN for retired government and private employees." "2027-04-01" "Tax Guides" "Pension Tax Guide" '<p class="article-lead">This guide explains income tax obligations for pensioners and retired persons in Pakistan for the tax year 2026. Many retirees are unsure whether their pension is taxable, whether they need to file a return, and how to maintain filer status after retirement. Kamboh Associates provides expert tax filing for pensioners at just Rs 3,500, handled entirely via WhatsApp.</p><h2 id="overview">Is Pension Taxable in Pakistan 2026?</h2><p>Under the Income Tax Ordinance 2001, pension income is treated differently depending on whether you are a government or private sector retiree. Government commutation and pension received by a government servant is fully exempt from income tax. Private sector employees are entitled to a partial exemption. However, if you have additional income sources like rent, bank profit, or investment returns, you must still file an annual return.</p><div class="warn-box"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i><p><strong>Important:</strong> Even if your pension is fully exempt from tax, you are still required to file an annual return and wealth statement if you own property worth over Rs 5 million, have a bank account with significant balance, or own a vehicle. Non-filing results in non-filer status and higher withholding tax on all transactions.</p></div><h2 id="obligations">Pension Tax Rules in Pakistan</h2><ul><li><strong>Government Pension</strong> - Fully exempt from income tax; commutation is also exempt</li><li><strong>Private Sector Pension</strong> - Exempt up to the statutory limit; consult a professional for exact amount applicable</li><li><strong>Gratuity</strong> - Exempt up to Rs 300,000 for private sector; fully exempt for government servants</li><li><strong>Bank Profit / Savings</strong> - Taxable; must be declared if you have a bank account</li><li><strong>Rental Income</strong> - Fully taxable; must be declared in your return</li><li><strong>Wealth Statement</strong> - Required if total assets exceed certain thresholds</li></ul><div class="info-grid"><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Govt Pension Tax</div><div class="value">Exempt</div><div class="sub">Fully exempt</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Pension Return Fee</div><div class="value">Rs 3,500</div><div class="sub">Same day filing</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">With Property/Rent</div><div class="value">From Rs 5,000</div><div class="sub">1-2 days</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Deadline</div><div class="value">30 September</div><div class="sub">Each tax year</div></div></div><h2 id="services">Our Services for Pensioners</h2><ul><li><strong>NTN Registration</strong> - Get your tax number quickly</li><li><strong>Pension Tax Return Filing</strong> - Correct exemption application</li><li><strong>Wealth Statement</strong> - Asset declaration done properly</li><li><strong>Rental Income Declaration</strong> - If you earn rent from property</li><li><strong>Bank Profit Declaration</strong> - Accurate treatment of profit income</li></ul><h2 id="pricing">Pricing</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Price</th><th>Timeline</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>NTN Registration</td><td>From Rs 1,500</td><td>24-48 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Pension Return (basic)</td><td>From Rs 3,500</td><td>Same day</td></tr><tr><td>Pension + Rental Income</td><td>From Rs 5,000</td><td>1-2 days</td></tr><tr><td>Wealth Statement</td><td>From Rs 5,000</td><td>2-3 days</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="article-cta"><h3>Pension Tax Filing - Fast and Simple</h3><p>WhatsApp your CNIC and pension details to 0328-4675162. We handle everything for you at Rs 3,500.</p><div class="cta-btns"><a href="https://wa.me/923284675162?text=Hi%2C+I+am+a+pensioner+and+need+tax+help." class="cta-btn-white" target="_blank"><i class="fab fa-whatsapp"></i> Free Consultation</a><a href="tel:03284675162" class="cta-btn-ghost"><i class="fas fa-phone"></i> 0328-4675162</a></div></div><h2 id="faqs">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">Does a retired government employee need to file income tax? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Yes, if you have other income like rent or bank profit, or own significant assets. Even with fully exempt pension, filing a return is required to stay on the ATL and avoid non-filer penalties on property transactions.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">Is gratuity received on retirement taxable in Pakistan? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Gratuity received by a government servant on retirement is fully exempt. For private sector employees, up to Rs 300,000 is exempt; the excess is taxable. A consultant ensures correct treatment.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">Can an elderly pensioner file their tax return remotely? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Yes. Simply WhatsApp your CNIC copy and basic details to 0328-4675162. Kamboh Associates files your return completely online. No office visit required.</div></div></div>'

Make-Blog "tax-consultant-private-job-pakistan" "Income Tax for Private Sector Employees Pakistan 2026" "Complete income tax guide for private company employees in Pakistan 2026. Salary tax slabs, WHT deduction, how to file return, NTN registration for private job holders." "2027-04-02" "Tax Guides" "Salaried Employee Tax" '<p class="article-lead">If you work in a private company in Pakistan, your employer deducts income tax (WHT) from your salary every month. But deduction alone does not fulfill your legal obligation. You must also file an annual income tax return and wealth statement by 30 September every year. Kamboh Associates handles this for private sector employees across Pakistan at just Rs 3,500, via WhatsApp.</p><h2 id="overview">Income Tax for Private Employees in Pakistan</h2><p>Under the Income Tax Ordinance 2001, all salaried individuals earning above Rs 600,000 per year (Rs 50,000 per month) are required to file an annual income tax return. Even those earning below this threshold should file to obtain NTN and maintain active filer status, which reduces withholding tax on property, vehicle, and banking transactions by up to 50%.</p><div class="info-box"><i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i><p><strong>Why Filing Matters Even With WHT:</strong> Your employer deducts tax on salary only. If you also earn bank profit, rent, or have other income, these must be declared in your annual return. Additionally, your wealth statement must reflect all assets including property, savings, and vehicles to avoid FBR notices.</p></div><h2 id="obligations">2026 Salary Tax Slabs for Pakistan</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Annual Income</th><th>Tax Rate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Up to Rs 600,000</td><td>0%</td></tr><tr><td>Rs 600,001 - Rs 1,200,000</td><td>5% of amount exceeding Rs 600,000</td></tr><tr><td>Rs 1,200,001 - Rs 2,200,000</td><td>Rs 30,000 + 15% of excess over Rs 1,200,000</td></tr><tr><td>Rs 2,200,001 - Rs 3,200,000</td><td>Rs 180,000 + 25% of excess over Rs 2,200,000</td></tr><tr><td>Rs 3,200,001 - Rs 4,100,000</td><td>Rs 430,000 + 30% of excess over Rs 3,200,000</td></tr><tr><td>Above Rs 4,100,000</td><td>Rs 700,000 + 35% of excess over Rs 4,100,000</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="services">Our Services for Private Employees</h2><ul><li><strong>NTN Registration</strong> - 24-48 hours, fully online</li><li><strong>Annual Salaried Tax Return</strong> - Quick filing with correct WHT reconciliation</li><li><strong>Wealth Statement</strong> - Accurate asset declaration</li><li><strong>FBR Notice Response</strong> - Professional handling</li><li><strong>Tax Refund Claims</strong> - Recover excess WHT deducted by employer</li></ul><h2 id="pricing">Pricing</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Price</th><th>Timeline</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>NTN Registration</td><td>From Rs 1,500</td><td>24-48 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Salaried Return</td><td>From Rs 3,500</td><td>Same day</td></tr><tr><td>Salary + Other Income</td><td>From Rs 5,000</td><td>1-2 days</td></tr><tr><td>Wealth Statement</td><td>From Rs 5,000</td><td>2-3 days</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="article-cta"><h3>File Your Salary Tax Return in One Day</h3><p>WhatsApp your salary certificate and CNIC to 0328-4675162. Done same day. Starting at Rs 3,500.</p><div class="cta-btns"><a href="https://wa.me/923284675162?text=Hi%2C+I+am+a+private+employee+and+need+to+file+my+tax+return." class="cta-btn-white" target="_blank"><i class="fab fa-whatsapp"></i> Free Consultation</a><a href="tel:03284675162" class="cta-btn-ghost"><i class="fas fa-phone"></i> 0328-4675162</a></div></div><h2 id="faqs">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">My employer already deducts income tax. Do I still need to file? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Yes. Your employer deducts WHT on salary only. You must file an annual return by 30 September to declare all income, submit a wealth statement, and stay on the ATL. Non-filing means non-filer status regardless of WHT deduction.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">What documents do I need to file my return as a private employee? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">You need your CNIC copy, salary certificate or payslip (showing annual salary and WHT deducted), bank profit certificate from your bank, and a list of assets. WhatsApp these to 0328-4675162 and we file same day.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">Can I get a refund if my employer deducted too much tax? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Yes. If the total WHT deducted by your employer exceeds your actual tax liability for the year, you can claim a refund by filing your return and submitting a refund application through FBR IRIS.</div></div></div>'

