Make-Blog "how-to-become-active-filer-pakistan-2026" "How to Become an Active Filer in Pakistan 2026 - Complete Guide" "Step-by-step guide to becoming an active filer in Pakistan in 2026. How to get on FBR ATL list, NTN registration, file income tax return, and check filer status online." "2027-04-03" "FBR" "FBR Filer Guide" '<p class="article-lead">Becoming an active filer in Pakistan saves you money on every major financial transaction. Active filers pay lower withholding tax on property purchases, vehicle registration, banking, and dividends. This step-by-step guide explains exactly how to get on the FBR Active Taxpayer List (ATL) in 2026 and how Kamboh Associates can complete the entire process for you in 24-48 hours.</p><h2 id="overview">What is an Active Filer (ATL) in Pakistan?</h2><p>The FBR Active Taxpayer List is a register of all individuals and businesses who have filed their income tax return for the previous tax year. Being on the ATL means you are an active filer and qualify for lower withholding tax rates on over 50 types of financial transactions. The ATL is updated weekly by FBR and published on the FBR website.</p><div class="info-grid"><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Property Purchase WHT</div><div class="value">3% vs 6%</div><div class="sub">Filer saves 3%</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Vehicle Registration</div><div class="value">50% Less</div><div class="sub">For filers</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Cash Withdrawal</div><div class="value">0.3% vs 0.6%</div><div class="sub">Filer vs non-filer</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Dividend Income</div><div class="value">15% vs 30%</div><div class="sub">Filer vs non-filer</div></div></div><h2 id="obligations">Step-by-Step: How to Become an Active Filer</h2><ol><li><strong>Get Your CNIC</strong> - You must have a valid CNIC to register on FBR IRIS</li><li><strong>Register on FBR IRIS</strong> - Go to iris.fbr.gov.pk, click "Registration for Unregistered Person" and complete the e-enrollment form with your CNIC, phone number, and email</li><li><strong>Receive Your NTN</strong> - After successful registration, FBR issues your National Tax Number (NTN) linked to your CNIC</li><li><strong>Prepare Your Documents</strong> - Gather your income details: salary certificate or business income, bank profit certificate, property/vehicle ownership details</li><li><strong>File Your Income Tax Return</strong> - Log in to FBR IRIS, select the relevant tax year return, fill in income and asset details, and submit</li><li><strong>Wait for ATL Update</strong> - FBR updates the ATL every Sunday. Your name appears within 3-7 days of filing</li><li><strong>Verify Your Status</strong> - Check your name on the FBR ATL at fbr.gov.pk/activetaxpayer/Login</li></ol><div class="info-box"><i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i><p><strong>Fastest Way:</strong> WhatsApp your CNIC copy to 0328-4675162. Kamboh Associates completes your NTN registration and files your return in 24-48 hours. Your ATL status activates within one week. No office visit, no FBR portal navigation needed.</p></div><div class="warn-box"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i><p><strong>Common Mistake:</strong> Simply registering NTN does NOT make you a filer. You must also file an income tax return for the relevant tax year. Many people register their NTN but forget to file the return, so they remain non-filers even with an NTN.</p></div><h2 id="services">Let Kamboh Associates Do It For You</h2><ul><li><strong>NTN Registration</strong> - Completed in 24-48 hours</li><li><strong>Income Tax Return Filing</strong> - Filed on FBR IRIS with all correct details</li><li><strong>Wealth Statement</strong> - Submitted with your return</li><li><strong>ATL Verification</strong> - We confirm your active status</li><li><strong>Total cost from Rs 3,500</strong> - Everything included</li></ul><h2 id="pricing">Pricing</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Price</th><th>Timeline</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>NTN Registration</td><td>From Rs 1,500</td><td>24-48 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Salaried Return + Filer Status</td><td>From Rs 3,500</td><td>Same day filing</td></tr><tr><td>Business Return + Filer Status</td><td>From Rs 7,000</td><td>2-3 days</td></tr><tr><td>ATL Surcharge (late filing)</td><td>Rs 1,000</td><td>Immediate</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="article-cta"><h3>Become an Active Filer in 48 Hours</h3><p>WhatsApp your CNIC to 0328-4675162. We register your NTN and file your return. Your ATL status activates within one week.</p><div class="cta-btns"><a href="https://wa.me/923284675162?text=Hi%2C+I+want+to+become+an+active+filer+in+Pakistan." class="cta-btn-white" target="_blank"><i class="fab fa-whatsapp"></i> Get Started Now</a><a href="tel:03284675162" class="cta-btn-ghost"><i class="fas fa-phone"></i> 0328-4675162</a></div></div><h2 id="faqs">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">How long does it take to become an active filer in Pakistan? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">After filing your income tax return, your name typically appears on the FBR ATL within 3-7 days. Kamboh Associates completes the NTN registration and return filing in 24-48 hours, so the full process takes about one week from start to ATL status.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">Can I become a filer without a salary or business income? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Yes. Even if you have no taxable income, you can file a nil return to get on the ATL. This is common for housewives, students, and individuals who want filer status for property or vehicle transactions.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">What is the ATL surcharge for late filers? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Individuals who missed the filing deadline can still get on the ATL by paying an ATL surcharge of Rs 1,000 and filing their return. After payment, ATL status is updated within days. Contact us to handle this process.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">How do I check if I am already on the FBR ATL? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Go to fbr.gov.pk and search Active Taxpayer List, then enter your CNIC number. Alternatively, WhatsApp your CNIC to 0328-4675162 and we check your status instantly for free.</div></div></div>'

Make-Blog "how-to-file-income-tax-return-fbr-iris-2026" "How to File Income Tax Return on FBR IRIS 2026 - Step by Step" "Complete step-by-step guide to filing income tax return on FBR IRIS portal in 2026. How to login, fill return form, submit wealth statement and get acknowledgment." "2027-04-04" "FBR" "FBR IRIS Filing Guide" '<p class="article-lead">This step-by-step guide explains how to file your income tax return on the FBR IRIS portal for the tax year 2025-26. Whether you are a salaried employee, business owner, or professional, this guide walks you through every step. If you prefer professional assistance, Kamboh Associates completes your return in 24-48 hours via WhatsApp at 0328-4675162.</p><h2 id="overview">What You Need Before You Start</h2><ul><li>CNIC number and FBR IRIS login credentials (NTN and password)</li><li>Salary certificate or business income details</li><li>Bank profit certificate from your bank</li><li>Details of all assets: property, vehicles, savings, investments</li><li>Withholding tax certificates from your employer or clients</li></ul><div class="warn-box"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i><p><strong>Filing Deadline:</strong> The income tax return for the tax year 2025-26 (July 2025 to June 2026) is due on 30 September 2026. Late filing results in a penalty of Rs 1,000 per day for individuals, up to a maximum of Rs 50,000.</p></div><h2 id="obligations">Step-by-Step Filing Guide</h2><ol><li><strong>Login to FBR IRIS</strong> - Go to iris.fbr.gov.pk. Enter your NTN (same as CNIC for individuals) and password. If you forgot your password, use the "Forgot Password" option with your registered mobile number.</li><li><strong>Navigate to Declarations</strong> - After login, click "Declaration" in the left menu, then select "114(1) Return of Income" for the relevant tax year.</li><li><strong>Select Return Type</strong> - Choose your income type: Salaried, Business, or Property. Most individuals select "Salaried" unless they have business income.</li><li><strong>Fill Personal Information</strong> - Verify your CNIC, name, and address details. Update if incorrect.</li><li><strong>Enter Salary Income</strong> - In the Salary section, enter your annual gross salary, total WHT deducted by your employer, and employer NTN. This information is on your salary certificate.</li><li><strong>Enter Other Income</strong> - Add bank profit (from your bank certificate), rental income, dividend income, and any other taxable income sources.</li><li><strong>Complete Wealth Statement</strong> - Declare all assets: residential property (with value), commercial property, vehicles (with registration and value), savings accounts, cash, investments, and foreign assets.</li><li><strong>Reconcile Expenditure</strong> - IRIS will calculate the difference between your income and asset additions. Ensure this reconciles; any unexplained increase in assets creates tax exposure.</li><li><strong>Submit Return</strong> - Review all entries, click "Submit." You receive a system-generated acknowledgment number confirming your filing.</li><li><strong>Verify ATL Status</strong> - Check the ATL within 3-7 days on the FBR website to confirm your filer status is active.</li></ol><div class="info-box"><i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i><p><strong>Save Time:</strong> The IRIS portal can be complex, especially for first-time filers or those with multiple income sources. WhatsApp your CNIC, salary certificate, and asset list to 0328-4675162. Kamboh Associates files your complete return in 24 hours, guaranteed correct.</p></div><h2 id="services">Common Mistakes to Avoid</h2><ul><li><strong>Forgetting bank profit</strong> - Banks report all profit to FBR; omitting it triggers discrepancies</li><li><strong>Under-declaring property value</strong> - Use FBR-notified values for property to avoid notices</li><li><strong>Incomplete wealth statement</strong> - All assets must be declared, not just property</li><li><strong>Wrong WHT entry</strong> - Cross-check your WHT figures with your IRIS tax ledger before entering</li><li><strong>Filing nil return when income exists</strong> - Filing incorrect returns can result in FBR notices</li></ul><h2 id="pricing">Professional Filing by Kamboh Associates</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Price</th><th>Timeline</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Salaried Return</td><td>From Rs 3,500</td><td>Same day</td></tr><tr><td>Business Return</td><td>From Rs 7,000</td><td>2-3 days</td></tr><tr><td>Property / Rental Income</td><td>From Rs 5,000</td><td>1-2 days</td></tr><tr><td>Wealth Statement</td><td>From Rs 5,000</td><td>2-3 days</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="article-cta"><h3>Let Us File Your Return - Done in 24 Hours</h3><p>WhatsApp your documents to 0328-4675162. We handle the entire IRIS filing professionally. Starts at Rs 3,500.</p><div class="cta-btns"><a href="https://wa.me/923284675162?text=Hi%2C+I+need+help+filing+my+income+tax+return+on+FBR+IRIS." class="cta-btn-white" target="_blank"><i class="fab fa-whatsapp"></i> File My Return Now</a><a href="tel:03284675162" class="cta-btn-ghost"><i class="fas fa-phone"></i> 0328-4675162</a></div></div><h2 id="faqs">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">What is the last date to file income tax return in Pakistan 2026? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">The deadline for filing income tax returns for tax year 2025-26 is 30 September 2026. Late filing attracts a penalty of Rs 1,000 per day. Contact us before the deadline to avoid penalties.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">I forgot my FBR IRIS password. How do I reset it? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">On the IRIS login page, click "Forgot Password" and enter your CNIC or NTN. A reset link is sent to your registered mobile number or email. If your registered contact details are outdated, contact FBR helpline at 051-111-772-772 or let Kamboh Associates handle it for you.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">How do I know if my return was filed successfully? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">After submission, IRIS generates an acknowledgment number. You can also check your return status in the "Declarations" section of IRIS. If filed successfully, the status shows "Submitted." Kamboh Associates sends you the acknowledgment screenshot immediately after filing.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">Can I file my return for previous years on FBR IRIS? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Yes. You can file returns for up to 5 previous tax years through FBR IRIS. Late filing for past years activates your ATL status for those years after payment of the applicable ATL surcharge.</div></div></div>'

Make-Blog "how-to-check-atl-status-pakistan" "How to Check ATL Status in Pakistan 2026 - FBR Active Taxpayer" "How to check your name on FBR Active Taxpayer List (ATL) in Pakistan 2026. Step-by-step guide to verify filer status online, by SMS, or mobile app. Check CNIC on ATL." "2027-04-05" "FBR" "ATL Status Check" '<p class="article-lead">The FBR Active Taxpayer List (ATL) shows who is a tax filer in Pakistan. Checking your ATL status takes less than 30 seconds using your CNIC. This guide shows three ways to verify filer status: online, by SMS, and via the Tax Asaan app. If your CNIC is not on the list, Kamboh Associates can get you on ATL within one week.</p><h2 id="overview">3 Ways to Check ATL Status in Pakistan</h2><h3>Method 1: Online at FBR Website</h3><ol><li>Go to <strong>fbr.gov.pk</strong></li><li>Click "Online Verification System" or search "Active Taxpayer List"</li><li>Enter your CNIC number (13 digits without dashes)</li><li>The result shows: Active Taxpayer, Inactive, or Not Found</li></ol><h3>Method 2: By SMS</h3><ol><li>Open your SMS app</li><li>Type your CNIC number (13 digits)</li><li>Send to <strong>9966</strong></li><li>You receive a reply: "ATL Status: Active/Inactive" with your name</li></ol><h3>Method 3: Tax Asaan Mobile App</h3><ol><li>Download "Tax Asaan" from Google Play or App Store</li><li>Go to "Taxpayer Profile" or "ATL Verification"</li><li>Enter CNIC to check status instantly</li></ol><div class="info-box"><i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i><p><strong>Quick Check for Someone Else:</strong> You can check the ATL status of any Pakistani citizen using their CNIC. This is useful when buying property, hiring contractors, or verifying vendor filer status before making payments to avoid higher WHT rates.</p></div><h2 id="obligations">What the ATL Result Means</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Result</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Action Required</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Active Taxpayer</td><td>You are on the ATL and a filer</td><td>None - you enjoy reduced WHT rates</td></tr><tr><td>Inactive</td><td>You have an NTN but did not file last year return</td><td>File your return immediately</td></tr><tr><td>Not Found</td><td>No NTN registered against this CNIC</td><td>Register NTN and file a return</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="warn-box"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i><p><strong>ATL Updates Weekly:</strong> FBR updates the ATL every Sunday. If you just filed your return, your status may take up to 7 days to reflect. The current ATL is based on returns filed for the last completed tax year.</p></div><h2 id="services">How to Get on the ATL if You Are Not Listed</h2><ul><li><strong>Step 1:</strong> Register your NTN on FBR IRIS (if you do not have one)</li><li><strong>Step 2:</strong> File your income tax return for the most recent tax year</li><li><strong>Step 3:</strong> Pay ATL surcharge of Rs 1,000 if filing is late</li><li><strong>Step 4:</strong> Wait 3-7 days for the next ATL update</li><li><strong>Fastest way:</strong> WhatsApp 0328-4675162 - Kamboh Associates handles the complete process</li></ul><h2 id="pricing">Pricing</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Price</th><th>Timeline</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>NTN Registration</td><td>From Rs 1,500</td><td>24-48 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Salaried Return + ATL</td><td>From Rs 3,500</td><td>Same day filing</td></tr><tr><td>ATL Surcharge Payment</td><td>Rs 1,000</td><td>Immediate</td></tr><tr><td>Business Return + ATL</td><td>From Rs 7,000</td><td>2-3 days</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="article-cta"><h3>Not on ATL? Get Listed in One Week</h3><p>WhatsApp your CNIC to 0328-4675162. We register NTN, file your return, and get you on the ATL. Rs 3,500 all-inclusive.</p><div class="cta-btns"><a href="https://wa.me/923284675162?text=Hi%2C+I+am+not+on+the+ATL+and+need+to+become+an+active+filer." class="cta-btn-white" target="_blank"><i class="fab fa-whatsapp"></i> Get on ATL Now</a><a href="tel:03284675162" class="cta-btn-ghost"><i class="fas fa-phone"></i> 0328-4675162</a></div></div><h2 id="faqs">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">How to check ATL status in Pakistan by SMS? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Send your 13-digit CNIC number (without dashes) as an SMS to 9966. You will receive a reply showing your Active Taxpayer List status: Active, Inactive, or Not Found.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">How long after filing does my name appear on the ATL? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">After filing your income tax return, your name typically appears on the ATL within 3-7 days, as FBR updates the list every Sunday. If you filed late and paid the ATL surcharge, it may update sooner.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">I have an NTN but I am not on the ATL. Why? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Having an NTN alone does not make you a filer. You must also file an income tax return for the latest tax year. Register your NTN and then file a return to appear on the ATL.</div></div></div>'

